# build output
dist/
# scratch checkout of the pages-content branch, made by scripts/publish-pages.sh
.pages-content/
# generated types
.astro/

# dependencies
node_modules/

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*


# environment variables
.env
.env.production

# macOS-specific files
.DS_Store

# Dropbox sync artifacts
*conflicted copy*
.dropbox
.dropbox.attr

# jetbrains setting folder
.idea/

# generator scratch: rebuilt by scripts/skymap-gen/gen.py on demand
scripts/skymap-gen/out.json

# python bytecode from scripts/pixel-qa
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# stray scratch files from the sandbox mount
_tmp_*

# Archived POC snapshots belong in archive/, never in public/.
# Anything in public/ is copied verbatim into dist/ and served raw: no password
# gate, no noindex, no review. public/mersive-website-poc.html was a v0.39
# snapshot doing exactly that, describing the SOC 2 attestation as "in progress
# per internal gap analysis" — an older claim than anything on the live pages.
public/*website-poc*.html
public/*-poc-*.html

# Insights imagery, re-hosted from other people's CDNs by
# scripts/fetch-blog-images.mjs — which the `build` script runs before astro,
# working from the INSIGHT_IMAGES manifest in src/data/insights.ts. That is 151
# files and ~22MB of pexels/WordPress stock nobody reviews or edits, and the
# fetch is idempotent, so a build produces them and a second build costs no
# requests. Nothing is lost by leaving them out: the pages fall back to the
# remote URL when the local copy is missing.
#
# Ignore the contents rather than the directory, so the re-includes below are
# reachable — git will not descend into an excluded directory.
public/blog/*
# Authored art, as opposed to fetched stock: keep it tracked. A new hand-made
# blog image must match one of these, or be added with `git add -f`.
!public/blog/embedded-*.webp
!public/blog/poc-*.png

# Polaris-Man audio working area.
#
# "Game audio files/" is a working folder, not a deliverable. It holds ~244MB
# that must not enter git: 175MB of Stability reference WAVs (two passes of 15,
# the raw material for the NES arrangements) and 68MB of archival NES masters
# rendered out of FamiStudio. Both are reproducible or already backed up
# elsewhere, and neither is served to anyone — the web build reads the OGGs in
# public/eggs/polaris-man/audio/, which ARE tracked.
#
# Ignore the contents rather than the directory so the re-includes below stay
# reachable: git will not descend into an excluded directory.
Game audio files/**
# The editable FamiStudio projects are the source of the soundtrack and are a
# few KB each. Losing them would mean the music could never be revised, only
# re-composed, so these are the one thing in here worth keeping.
!Game audio files/
!Game audio files/Polaris Man/
!Game audio files/Polaris Man/nes/
!Game audio files/Polaris Man/nes/famistudio/
!Game audio files/Polaris Man/nes/famistudio/*.txt
# The generation manifest records prompts, seeds and generation IDs for the
# reference batch — provenance, and small.
!Game audio files/Polaris Man/Polaris-Man-Audio-Generation-Manifest.md
!Game audio files/Polaris Man/audio_prompt.txt

# Mars: Signal Siege working folders.
#
# Same reasoning as the Polaris-Man block above, applied to the second Phaser
# egg. What the site actually serves lives in public/eggs/mars-signal-siege/ and
# IS tracked; these are the working materials behind it.
#
# "Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/source-local" is 45MB of painterly Mersive
# masters, copied in from the Mars deliverables folder rather than authored
# here. "source-cdn" is 4.6MB re-fetched from the Phaser Game Agent's asset
# host. Both are reproducible — source-cdn from the tracked manifest below,
# source-local from Dropbox — and neither is served to anyone.
Game art files/**
# The Aseprite masters ARE authored here and are a few KB each. Losing them
# would mean the three enemy types could never be revised, only redrawn.
!Game art files/
!Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/
!Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/aseprite/
!Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/aseprite/*.aseprite
!Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/aseprite/*.json
!Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/exports/
!Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/exports/*
# Provenance: records the source URL for every CDN-recovered asset, so the
# 4.6MB can be re-fetched exactly rather than guessed at.
!Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/source-cdn/
!Game art files/Mars Signal Siege/source-cdn/_cdn_manifest.json

# Mars audio: the 93MB of WAV masters and the FamiStudio renders are already
# excluded by the "Game audio files/**" rule above. Re-include the editable
# chip project and the loop-point record, for the same reason Polaris-Man keeps
# its FamiStudio text projects.
!Game audio files/Mars Signal Siege/
!Game audio files/Mars Signal Siege/famistudio/
!Game audio files/Mars Signal Siege/famistudio/*.txt
!Game audio files/Mars Signal Siege/loop-points.json

# Mars QA scratch: regenerable audit renders from the art build and the
# runtime harness. The few sheets worth keeping are exported to docs/mars-shots.
docs/mars-qa/
